  data: {
    LLM: "1. The lead player plays a card.\n2. In turn, others play ANY card. You do not have to follow suit.\n3. **Winning the Trick**: To beat the lead, you must play a card of the SAME RANK as the lead, or a WILD card (7 or 2).\n4. **Countering**: The lead player can respond by playing another card of the same rank or another wild card to 'take back' the trick. This continues until everyone has passed or played on the lead.\n5. The last player to match the lead rank (or play a wild) wins all cards in the trick.",
    Player: "1. The lead player plays a card.\n2. In turn, others play ANY card. You do not have to follow suit.\n3. **Winning the Trick**: To beat the lead, you must play a card of the SAME RANK as the lead, or a WILD card (7 or 2).\n4. **Countering**: The lead player can respond by playing another card of the same rank or another wild card to 'take back' the trick. This continues until everyone has passed or played on the lead.\n5. The last player to match the lead rank (or play a wild) wins all cards in the trick.",
    objective: "Score points by capturing Aces and Tens (the 'counting cards'). There are 90 total points available (8 counting cards + 10 for the last trick).",
    gameplay: "1. The lead player plays a card.\n2. In turn, others play ANY card. You do not have to follow suit.\n3. **Winning the Trick**: To beat the lead, you must play a card of the SAME RANK as the lead, or a WILD card (7 or 2).\n4. **Countering**: The lead player can respond by playing another card of the same rank or another wild card to 'take back' the trick. This continues until everyone has passed or played on the lead.\n5. The last player to match the lead rank (or play a wild) wins all cards in the trick.",
